# These pages carried Cache-Control: no-transform until 2026-08-13. It was
# added because Cloudflare's JavaScript Detections beacon kept injecting into
# every page even with Bot Fight Mode off -- a state the Free plan exposes no
# control for -- which made the primary site fail its own manifest.json
# verification while every mirror passed.
#
# The cost turned out to be much larger than the "few KB each" originally
# assumed: no-transform also forbids the edge from compressing, so all twelve
# pages shipped uncompressed. Measured across nine live pages, the correlation
# was exact -- the only two pages without the directive were the only two
# Cloudflare compressed. Removing it saves roughly 138 KB site-wide and 6.8 KB
# on the home page alone, about 14% of a cold visit.
#
# Safe to remove because the premise no longer reproduces: a page Cloudflare
# was free to transform came back byte-identical to the local build apart from
# the build stamp, with no beacon anywhere in it. And if injection ever
# returns, this site detects it by construction -- the primary would fail
# manifest verification while the mirrors passed, which is exactly how it was
# caught the first time.
# Onion-Location tells Tor Browser that an onion service carries the same page,
# so it can offer the .onion instead. Tor requires the advertising page to be
# HTTPS, which Cloudflare Pages and Netlify both are. Paths are listed one by
# one so each page points at its own onion equivalent rather than the homepage.
/
